.TH GH-BOARD 1 "2026-09-05" "gh-board 0.17.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gh-board \- GitHub terminal dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gh-board
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ URL ]
.br
.B gh-board
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ COMMAND-OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gh-board
is an interactive terminal dashboard for GitHub pull requests, issues,
notifications, workflow runs, security alerts, and repository branches.
It uses the repository detected from the current working directory when
appropriate and can also operate across all configured repositories.
.PP
The dashboard is navigated with the keyboard.  Press
.B ?
to display contextual help.  Press
.B 1
through
.B 6
to select a view, or
.B n
and
.B N
to cycle through views.
.PP
A GitHub pull request, issue, or Actions run URL may be supplied directly as a
shorthand for the
.B open
command.  The explicit form is preferred when scripting or documenting a
command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load only the specified TOML configuration file.  This bypasses normal
configuration-file discovery.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging and write logs to
.I ./debug.log
instead of the normal cache log.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.TP
.I URL
A GitHub pull request, issue, or Actions run URL.  This is shorthand for
.BR "gh-board open URL" .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
Initialize a new configuration file interactively.  The wizard generates a
starter configuration for the current user.
.SS themes
List the names of all built-in themes, one per line.
.SS config
Show the resolved configuration after all applicable configuration layers have
been merged.  Values are printed as
.IR key = value .
.TP
.B \-\-show-origin
Prefix each entry with the source file and a tab, in the form
.IR file:path " (tab) " key = value .
.SS open
Open a GitHub URL directly in its corresponding view.
.TP
.I URL
A pull request, issue, or Actions run URL.  Both github.com and GitHub
Enterprise hosts are supported.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is written in TOML.  Unless
.B \-\-config
is used, files are loaded in this order:
.IP 1. 3
Global configuration: the file named by
.BR $GH_BOARD_CONFIG ,
then
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gh-board/config.toml ,
then
.BR $HOME/.config/gh-board/config.toml .
.IP 2. 3
Ancestor configuration: each
.I gh-board.toml
or
.I .gh-board.toml
between the user's home directory and the Git repository root, from the
farthest ancestor inward.
.IP 3. 3
Project configuration:
.I gh-board.toml
or
.I .gh-board.toml
at the Git repository root.
.PP
Later layers override earlier layers.  Filter lists replace an earlier list
when the later list is non-empty; repository paths are merged, with closer
entries taking precedence.  A
.B theme_file
may name a built-in theme with the
.B builtin:
prefix or point to a theme-only TOML file.  Inline theme settings override
the theme file.
.PP
The example configuration is available at
.I examples/config.toml
in the source repository.  See also
.I FILTERS.md
for PR, issue, Actions, alerts, and notification filter syntax, and
.I KEYBINDINGS.md
for keybinding customization.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Authentication is resolved separately for each GitHub host.  The following
sources are tried in order:
.IP 1. 3
The GitHub CLI command
.BR "gh auth token --hostname HOST" .
.IP 2. 3
The
.B GH_TOKEN
environment variable.
.IP 3. 3
The
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
environment variable.
.PP
Install and authenticate the GitHub CLI with
.BR "gh auth login" ,
or set one of the token environment variables before starting
.BR gh-board .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GH_BOARD_CONFIG
Path to a global configuration file.  Used when the file exists.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the global configuration file
.IR gh-board/config.toml .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the normal log file
.IR gh-board/gh-board.log .
If unset, the cache directory defaults to
.IR $HOME/.cache/gh-board .
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN
GitHub authentication token.  Takes precedence over
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN ,
but not over a token returned by the GitHub CLI.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Fallback GitHub authentication token.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter used for log output.  If unset, the default level is
.B warn
or
.B debug
when
.B \-\-debug
is supplied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/gh-board/config.toml
Default global configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gh-board/config.toml
XDG global configuration file.
.TP
.I gh-board.toml
Project or ancestor configuration file.
.TP
.I .gh-board.toml
Alternative project or ancestor configuration filename.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gh-board/gh-board.log
Normal warning-and-above log file.
.TP
.I ./debug.log
Debug log file created with
.BR \-\-debug .
.TP
.I ./panic.log
Panic report written when the fullscreen interface encounters a panic.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
The default controls include:
.IP \(bu 2
.BR j / k
or the arrow keys to move through items.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR h / l
or the arrow keys to change filter tabs.
.IP \(bu 2
.B p
to toggle the preview pane.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR r / R
to refresh the selected item or current filter.
.IP \(bu 2
.B o
to open the selected item in a browser.
.IP \(bu 2
.B q
to quit.
.PP
Keybindings can be replaced or extended in the
.B [keybindings]
configuration section.  Custom shell commands may use item template variables
such as
.B {{.Url}}
and
.B {{.RepoName}}.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the dashboard using discovered configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gh-board
.fi
.RE
.PP
Open a pull request directly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gh-board open https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/42
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a specific configuration file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gh-board --config ~/config/gh-board.toml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect the merged configuration and its origins:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gh-board config --show-origin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run as a GitHub CLI extension:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gh board
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gh (1),
.UR https://github.com/graelo/gh-board
project documentation
.UE
